    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>(B)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math></p><p>(D)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math></p><p>Higher the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> value, higher the energy of the orbital and if two orbitals have same <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;value, then the orbital with higher <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> value has higher&nbsp;energy.</p><p>Thus:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>"
